0..76 Comment "//! Dybjer and Setzer\'s signatures for inductive-recursive definitions, with"
77..151 Comment "//! the family a signature defines and its decoder, read through `std.ir`."
152..155 Comment "//!"
156..229 Comment "//! A signature describes a family and its decoder at once. It asks for a"
230..305 Comment "//! value of a type, for values of the family, or for a stop. The values of"
306..375 Comment "//! the family come through their decodes. A stop names one decode. A"
376..447 Comment "//! function computes the type of these arguments from the signature. A"
448..512 Comment "//! family and its decoder thus follow from the signature alone."
513..516 Comment "//!"
517..594 Comment "//! The signatures are a large type. A field of a signature holds a type. The"
595..667 Comment "//! pairs are data, and `args` returns them as terms by recursion on the"
668..744 Comment "//! signature. The family a signature defines is `IR(d, c)`, and its decoder"
745..818 Comment "//! is `el(d, c, m)`. Its one constructor `Intro` holds the arguments the"
819..894 Comment "//! signature asks for over the family itself. The pathological twin\'s `Mu`"
895..971 Comment "//! and `decodeMu` write the same pair as ordinary source, and stay refused."
972..975 Comment "//!"
976..1053 Comment "//! - owes: #5160 — the eliminator of the family, with its computation rule"
1054..1133 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/universe/ir-codes.gandr` — the family a code defines"
1134..1198 Comment "//!   and its decoder, refused, over the decode of its arguments"
1199..1278 Comment "//! - cites: [Dybjer-1999-finite_axiomatization_inductiverecursive_definitions]"
1279..1282 Comment "//!"
1283..1475 Comment "//! [Dybjer-1999-finite_axiomatization_inductiverecursive_definitions]: https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-48959-2_11 \"Dybjer and Setzer, A finite axiomatization of inductive-recursive definitions\""
